        "name": "logan_mann",
        "username": "logan_mann",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/43a26b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-04-17T17:59:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Okay, working on the heroes...</p><p>Chrono-Ranger done. He has a couple I assume are one shots though they don't say it like the other comics usually show.</p><p>Omnitron-X done. Reminded me that one of my biggest puzzles I can't unpuzzle is the Fanatic Apostate First Appearaance mystery. they are quoted in back to back issues in one comic, one being Fanatics First Appearance...but His First appearance is issue 24 of a title in her name which MUST have come after her own First Appearance. Cant get my mind around that one.</p><p>The Scholar done. Man he is everywhere. Seems like he has mentored and helped many other heroes find their path. Expatriatte, The Wraith, Argent Adept, Haka...he's all over. And he also adds to the Fanatic Apostate mystery with Fanatic being quoted on one of his cards 80 issues before her First Appearance as listed on the website. Mystery Comics is really a mystery to me.</p><p>Looked through The Dreamer quickly to see if she'd take long.&nbsp; I don't even know where to start with her.&nbsp; She's got quotes on her cards from other characters all over the board. (It was confirmed that a quote on a card by someone other then the decks main character did show they were also present in that issue. She's quoted in Freedom Five Annual #4. That puts the Dreamer in WAY before the Visionary ever first appears (later in that same comic) but many of the quotes by others in the comic would put them before their own First Appearance dates...like the quote from Unity.</p><p>Did the Dreamer enter comics before The Visionary ever did? Or when she was created later was it revealed that years worth of unexplained events were actually connected and all came from this little girl? Do her dreams transend time as well?</p><p>Not even sure where to go with this now.&nbsp; Might try the others and come back to her.</p>",
        "post_number": 80,
        "post_type": 1,
