        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pwatson1974/{size}/1925_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-04-18T13:50:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The quotes source file is attached.</p><p>I figure that the Dreamer's projections have a much longer history and appearance in the comics than she does. I also suspect that the earlier than first appearances are off panel 'appearances' such as a shadowy figure for Apostate. Fanastic could be Helena reporting whatr she saw the Scholar do before it's revealed she's Fanatic. Although then, I'd presume the quote would be for Helena. Possibly another quote that is only later revealed to be her so it doesn't count against her first recognised appearance.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Also, a theory that I haven't seen, probably because it's obvious to everyone, but it looks like Absolution is the renaming/renumbering of Fanatic and is her 'Redeemer' series. I say this as we know from Apostate's backstory that his appearance maanges to shock Fanatic and make her doubt her faith. Given he appears in the highest three issue numbers, so far, of the Fanatic series it seems that this is the storyline that brings about the fall of Fanatic. The quote of Absolution&nbsp; also has a very \"I have fallen and will now climb back up\" feel to them. Plus, absolution and redemption are close concepts, so it seems reasonable that there is a link (at least to me). If I had to guess, I'd place A Day in the life: Fanartic between them as that quote has a very down and near defeat air to it. This is just thoughts rather than anything concrete, of course.</p>\n<p><a class=\"attachment\" href=\"/uploads/short-url/efvIoaUjBdA5TOkvJoHQEBBL0a4.xlsx\">Quotes sources.xlsx</a> (20.5 KB)</p>",
