      {
        "id": 38574,
        "name": "jkl620",
        "username": "jkl620",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/a9adbd/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-06-16T17:10:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Katsue\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/katsue/48/2012_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Katsue:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Looking at Miss Information's deck, I would tentatively place the Administrative Assassin series before Freedom Five Annual 21. There's nothing in the AA quotes to indicate that Aminia Twain has revealed herself.An alternative possibility, of course, is that Administrative Assassin is a retelling of Freedom Five Annual <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#21</span>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I just got done playing a game using the Miss Information Villian deck. I laid them out by quote and it looks like it is all one story arc. Freedom Five <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#657</span> Introduces the limited run series of Administrative Assassin and the story culminates in Freedom Five Annual <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#21</span>.</p>\n<p>I think the spreadsheet should have FF <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#657</span>, AA <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#1-5</span> and FFAnnual <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#21</span> all in the same year.</p>\n<p>edit-spelling</p>",
